# Voice trigger lab ("salvar" detector). Field recordings, converted audio and anything derived from them stay local (GBs,
# and they hold other people's voices and conversations).
# Allow-list: only this file, the reports, the lab scripts, the result tables and the VoiceBench app's sources go to git;
# anything new is ignored by default.
*
!.gitignore
!*.md
!lab/
!lab/tools/
!lab/tools/*.py
!lab/tools/results/
!lab/tools/results/*.csv
!lab/ios-bench/
!lab/ios-bench/**

# Kept local on purpose (regenerated by the scripts, see the report's "Reproduce"):
#   <date>/                    original clips and watch recordings
#   lab/wav16/                 16 kHz WAV copies
#   lab/tools/marks/           VAD + Whisper transcripts (include bystanders' talk)
#   lab/tools/models/          prototype classifiers (.pkl)
#   lab/tools/oww/, lab/tools/sherpa-onnx-whisper-small/   downloaded models
#   lab/tools/build/           export_detector.py's Core ML package
lab/ios-bench/VoiceBench/Data/
lab/ios-bench/**/xcuserdata/
lab/ios-bench/**/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
.DS_Store

__pycache__/
